                            <Interaction>
                                <Abbreviated/>
                                <Professional>Disulfiram may increase the anticoagulant effect of warfarin via an unclear mechanism. Two case reports of prolonged prothrombin time were noted in patients on concurrent disulfiram and warfarin. One of the reports described that the patient experienced several bleeding occasions such as haematuria, epistaxis and subconjunctival haemorrhage. Studies in healthy subjects found increased prothrombin time and warfarin plasma level. The authors suggested that disulfiram may have affected the hepatic metabolism of warfarin. Monitor patient’s INR and observe for signs of bleeding during combined use.</Professional>
